# The raw chain database. Untracked since 2026-11-22: Git LFS stores a
# complete new copy of a SQLite file on every push, which took the quota to
# 9.01GB of an included 10GB while the daily growth rate never changed. It
# is published as a release asset instead and fetched with
# `python -m src.chain_release download` -- see that module for the whole
# story. Ignored rather than merely deleted so a stray `git add` cannot put
# 658MB back into the repository.
database/schwab_database.db
database/schwab_database.db.download

# Local-only databases. Point a local dev session at one of these via
# SCHWAB_DB_PATH so a live refresh never writes over the downloaded copy:
#
#   export SCHWAB_DB_PATH=database/local.db
#
database/local*.db
database/*.local.db
demo-data/

# Backups written by src/backfill_session_dates.py --apply. ~658MB each, so
# an accidental `git add` would put 658MB of binary into git proper --
# painful to undo, and nothing in this repo is LFS-tracked any more to
# soften it. They are your undo for the relabelling; delete them once the
# result is verified and published.
*.pre-backfill
